      "settings": {
        "heading": "Press",
        "intro": "<p>Everything you need to write about us, in one place—numbers, names and a few story angles, all free to use editorially with a credit. Need hi-res images, samples or an interview? Just ask: we're two blokes and an inbox, so you'll get a real reply.</p>",
        "press_email": "",
        "boiler_heading": "The short version",
        "boilerplate": "<p>Whisky Blender lets anyone blend, name and label their own bottle of Scotch. Founded in Bothwell, Scotland in 2011 by two friends, Andy and Drew, it hand-selects well-aged casks and hands the blending over to the customer—who then names the result and puts it on the label. Every bottle is filled and bottled in Scotland. In fifteen years more than 45,000 people have designed their own whisky and over 7,700 have had it bottled: for weddings, for birthdays, for wakes, and for folk who just fancied one with their own name on it.</p>",
        "stats_heading": "By the numbers",
        "stats_intro": "<p>We've kept records since 2011, which means we can tell you a few things nobody else can about what people do when you hand them a bottle of Scotch and let them name it.</p>",
        "names_heading": "A few of the names",
        "names_intro": "<p>Every bottle is named by the person who made it. These are all real, and they are our favourites. Happy to dig out more on request.</p>",
        "angles_heading": "Things we can help with",
        "facts_heading": "Fast facts",
        "assets_heading": "Images",
        "assets_note": "Hi-res, unwatermarked, and free to use editorially with a credit to Whisky Blender.",
        "founders_heading": "Who to talk to",
        "coverage_heading": "Previously in",
        "contact_heading": "Get in touch",
        "contact_text": "<p>Press enquiries, images, samples, interviews, or a daft question about casks—all welcome. We can usually turn things round the same day.</p><p>Happy to send a bottle to anyone writing about us. Tell us what you want it called and we'll put it on the label.</p>"
      }
